## Comparison of the LWO and adjusted PIM methods using the proportional odds model to simulate data

## Difference between the methods:

## - They only consider comparisons between observations at the same visit, 
##   including comparisons between observations from the same treatment group
##
## - They obtain parameter estimates are obtained using GEE (where the grouping variable is based on unqiue id pairs)->NOTE: when 
##    e.g. AR1 is used, also these parameter estimates are different from the PIM estimates
##
## - Using these parameter estimates, they construct the U matrix and calculate the correct var-covar matrix using the "phi" indicator,
##   which equals 1 when PO are linked to same indiciduals (exactly the same as adjusted PIM)
##
##
##    NOTE: the standard errors of the estimated group effects at each visit are equal for both approaches (i.e. LWO and adjusted PIM) 
##    and also equal to the unadjusted PIM; However, the covariances are different for the original PIM!!!! This is important when 
##    testing interaction effects in our adjusted PIM method with model 2
##

